- Assume "mouse.X" and "mouse.Y" refer to the mouse's current X and Y position, respectively
- Assume "pinn.X" and "pinn.Y" refer to the pinn's current X and Y positiom, respectively

[Mouse Listener Function]
- When left mouse button is pressed:
  - If on empty board, do nothing
  - If on text, run [Text Editing Function] (defined elsewhere)
  - If directly on edges/corners, run [Pinn Resizing Function] (defined elsewhere)
  - If anywhere else on the Pinn, run [Pinn Movement Function]

[Pinn Movement Function]
- Subtract the mouse.X from pinn.X, store as "xOffset"
- Subtract the mouse.Y from pinn.Y, store as "yOffset"
- Repeat every frame (or whenever cursor movement is detected, whichever ends up fitting project framework better):
  - If left mouse button is no longer pressed, exit loop, otherwise:
    - Update pinn.X to mouse.X + xOffset
    - Update pinn.Y to mouse.Y + yOffset
    - Redraw UI (if not handled elsewhere)
- Inform autosave function that a Pinn's data has been updated (if autosaving whenever a Pinn is changed)
